:name: Anchor
:description: Anchor bootloader on an emulated STM32F746, with signed images in the flash slots.

# Usual way to run this: python3 tools/run.py   (see the README)
# Directly:              renode renode/anchor.resc
#
# $ORIGIN is the folder this script is in, so it works from any directory.
# The three variables below can be set before including the script, to try
# other files; that is what tools/run.py does.

$boot   ?= $ORIGIN/../bin/anchor
$slot_a ?= $ORIGIN/../build/slot_a.img
$slot_b ?= $ORIGIN/empty_slot.bin

using sysbus
mach create "anchor"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $ORIGIN/anchor.repl

# The bootloader is an ELF file: Renode places it at its link address
# (0x08000000) and starts the CPU from its vector table.
sysbus LoadELF $boot

# Images are raw bytes written at the base of a slot, as a flash
# programmer would do. By default slot B gets a few zero bytes: empty.
sysbus LoadBinary $slot_a 0x08040000
sysbus LoadBinary $slot_b 0x08080000

# Print everything the UART says in the Renode log.
showAnalyzer usart1 Antmicro.Renode.Analyzers.LoggingUartAnalyzer

start
